From ba6579a3d0edf3c8a8af30fcb434ea6e2cc5a3f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:40:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: flush deferred scan done message on interface
 down

When an interface goes down while a scan is running, the netdev
notifier completes the scan with ___cfg80211_scan_done(rdev, false).
That releases cfg80211's view of the request and stores the scan done
netlink message in rdev->scan_msg. Only the next ___cfg80211_scan_done()
call sends and clears that message, and until then every new scan is
rejected with -EBUSY.

That next call used to come from the driver: completing the cancelled
scan queued scan_done_wk. Since commit dab68a74e90b ("wifi: cfg80211:
don't free driver-owned scan requests"), a request the driver still
owns is only marked stale, and cfg80211_scan_done() frees it and
returns without queueing the work. The deferred message is then never
sent and scanning stays blocked until the wiphy is unregistered.

This is easy to hit with drivers that complete a cancelled hardware
scan asynchronously. With wcn36xx (firmware scan offload) it happens
whenever NetworkManager brings the interface down during a scan, for
example to apply a stable cloned MAC address when reconnecting. All
later scan requests fail and wpa_supplicant logs

  wlan0: CTRL-EVENT-SCAN-FAILED ret=-16 retry=1

until the driver module is reloaded.

Queue scan_done_wk when the message is deferred, so that it is
delivered regardless of when the driver completes the stale request.

This change was developed with an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5)
during LG Fx0 bring-up. The assistant found the problem, wrote the change
and this message, and ran the tests described above.

Fixes: dab68a74e90b ("wifi: cfg80211: don't free driver-owned scan requests")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/wireless/scan.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/wireless/scan.c b/net/wireless/scan.c
index d35c826c4b1a..aacb909e9b6b 100644
--- a/net/wireless/scan.c
+++ b/net/wireless/scan.c
@@ -1194,10 +1194,18 @@ void ___cfg80211_scan_done(struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev,
 	cfg80211_put_scan_req(rdev->scan_req);
 	rdev->scan_req = NULL;
 
-	if (!send_message)
-		rdev->scan_msg = msg;
-	else
+	if (send_message) {
 		nl80211_send_scan_msg(rdev, msg);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The interface is going down; defer the message to the worker.
+	 * A driver that still owns the request no longer queues the worker
+	 * when it completes, so do it here or new scans stay blocked.
+	 */
+	rdev->scan_msg = msg;
+	wiphy_work_queue(&rdev->wiphy, &rdev->scan_done_wk);
 }
 
 void __cfg80211_scan_done(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wiphy_work *wk)
-- 
2.56.0

